  "specId": "e8af190b-flow-query-api",
  "issue": 517,
  "request": "Issue #517: a704: [ENHANCE] [Flow Foundation Reorganization 11/12] Expose the Flow query API for Workspace\n\nGoal: Add a read-only public query API at sennel flow query so Workspace / Connector can retrieve the canonical Flow Version without depending on the internal filesystem layout.\n\nScope: Accept exactly one JSON request object from stdin or --request-file, validate resource-specific contracts, discover and select a canonical Flow Version, and return query-specific Schema Revision 1 JSON only on stdout. Support metadata for one selected Flow Version and activities for its confirmed Activity sequence. Require one specId; default omitted flowVersion to Version 1 and never fall back implicitly. Return selectedFlowVersion and ascending availableFlowVersions. Project current Flow state, Spec, public Artifact metadata and deterministic IDs, relations, authority-backed timestamps, derived blocked state, next action/recovery, and measured aggregate metrics. Project Activities with identity, timing, usage, outcome, failure/blocker/incomplete, metrics/notes, evaluation/finding/repair/Artifact references, ordered by confirmationOrder. Support recordedAt gte/lt filtering, opaque cursor pagination with query binding and cursor validation, stable resource-specific error shapes, and non-zero CLI exit on ok:false. Use the same reader/validator for fresh and migrated Flows; support active, parked, blocked-derived, finalized fixtures, with and without Git. Keep error codes and JSON Schema centrally managed and test consumer compatibility and read-only preservation of canonical files and the Git working tree.\n\nOut of scope: Workspace-specific view models, Artifact bodies, raw logs, prompts, internal paths, raw catalog, cross-Spec/full-text/arbitrary-sort/offset/aggregate queries, Flow Version creation/increment, Version 2 creation, old-layout parsing, migration reports, backward-compatible fallback, and any query-side update to Flow state, Activity, Artifact, cache, or Git.\n\nAcceptance: stdin and --request-file work with JSON-only stdout; metadata returns item and activities returns items/pageInfo without cardinality/order in requests; active/parked/finalized succeed and blocked is derived; datetime filtering uses Activity timing.finishedAt rather than filesystem timestamps; pagination has no gaps/duplicates and rejects reuse outside its query; finalized results are stable and active cursor positions survive appends; fresh start time comes from flow_created and migrated Flows without evidence return unavailable with reason/provenance; public relations work without internal paths or bodies; invalid/nonexistent/unreadable/inconsistent input produces no partial success and stable resource-specific errors; Version 2+ fixtures are queryable without Version 1 hardcoding; execution leaves canonical files and Git working tree unchanged.\n\nDependencies: 597f (artifact contract), b9b4 (canonical runtime), 900a (migration), eee7 (Git tracking boundary).",
